{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"diagnosis\":\"The proof is missing. Differentiate the first-time-derivative equation supplied by the extrema condition, use Faraday’s identity and commutation of time/space derivatives to expand the magnetic term, then differentiate Gauss’s law to replace the gradient of the electric divergence by the charge-density gradient. Finally use c² = (μ₀ε₀)⁻¹ and normalize the field coefficients.\",\"proof_body\":\"by\\n  have hmax :=\\n    (isExtrema_iff_gauss_ampere_magneticFieldMatrix hA J hJ).mp h\\n  have hamp :\\n      (fun s => ∂ₜ (A.electricField 𝓕.c · x i) s) =\\n        fun s =>\\n          1 / (𝓕.μ₀ * 𝓕.ε₀) *\\n              ∑ j, ∂[j] (A.magneticFieldMatrix 𝓕.c s · (j, i)) x -\\n            (1 / 𝓕.ε₀) * J.currentDensity 𝓕.c s x i := by\\n    funext s\\n    exact time_deriv_electricField_of_isExtrema hA J hJ h s x i\\n  have hamp' := congrArg (fun f : Time → ℝ => ∂ₜ f t) hamp\\n  have hgauss :\\n      (fun y => ∑ j, ∂[j] (A.electricField 𝓕.c t · j) y) =\\n        fun y => J.chargeDensity 𝓕.c t y / 𝓕.ε₀ := by\\n    funext y\\n    simpa using (hmax t y).1\\n  have hgauss' := congrArg (fun f : Space d → ℝ => ∂[i] f x) hgauss\\n  simp (disch := fun_prop)\\n      [time_deriv_magneticFieldMatrix A (hA.of_le (ENat.LEInfty.out)),\\n        Space.deriv_eq_fderiv_basis, Space.deriv_commute,\\n        Finset.sum_sub_distrib] at hamp' hgauss'\\n  linear_combination (norm := field_simp [FreeSpace.c_sq]) hamp' -\\n    (𝓕.c ^ 2) * hgauss'\"}"}}
